{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Eatza Pizza was a buffet-style restaurant chain founded in Arizona in 1997.","title":"Eatza Pizza"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" As recently as 2007, it was one of the largest all-buffet pizza chains in the United States, with 112 locations in 14 states and Puerto Rico.","title":"Eatza Pizza"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Upper Crust Pizzeria is a Boston, Massachusetts based chain of pizzeria restaurants.","title":"Upper Crust Pizzeria"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The chain went bankrupt following a finding by the U.S. Department of Labor that it had engaged in wage theft (not paying workers their legally required wages).","title":"Upper Crust Pizzeria"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"California-style pizza (also known as California pizza or Gourmet pizza) is a style of single-serving pizza that combines New York and Italian thin crust with toppings from the California cuisine cooking style.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Its invention is generally attributed to chef Ed LaDou, and Chez Panisse, in Berkeley, California.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Wolfgang Puck, after meeting LaDou, popularized the style of pizza in the rest of the country.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is served in a number of California Cuisine restaurants.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Such restaurant chains as California Pizza Kitchen, Extreme Pizza, and Sammy's Woodfired Pizza are three major pizza franchises associated with California-style pizza.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Nancy Silverton's Pizzeria Mozza is also a popular California-style pizza restaurant in Los Angeles.","title":"California-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lou Malnati's Pizzeria is an American Chicago-style pizza restaurant chain headquartered in Northbrook, Illinois.","title":"Lou Malnati's Pizzeria"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was founded by the son of Rudy Malnati, who was instrumental in developing the recipe for Chicago-style pizza, and it has become one of the Chicago area's best-known local lines of pizza restaurants.","title":"Lou Malnati's Pizzeria"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Lou Malnati's operates a division of its company called Lou Malnati's Presents Tastes of Chicago, a partnership with Portillo's Restaurants and Eli's Cheesecake, which ships Chicago-style cuisine nationally.","title":"Lou Malnati's Pizzeria"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Basin and range topography is an alternating landscape of parallel mountain ranges and valleys.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a result of crustal extension/stretching (extensional tectonics) of the lithosphere (crust and upper mantle) due to mantle upwelling, gravitational collapse, crustal thickening, or relaxation of confining stresses.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Crustal extension causes the thinning and deformation of the upper crust in an orientation perpendicular to the direction of extension.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As the plates pull apart, they thin allowing the hot mantle to rise close to the surface.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" When the crust is extended it fractures along a fault plane, creating a series of long parallel normal faults. Between these normal faults are blocks, which subside, get uplifted or tilted.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" This is known as block faulting.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Basins are formed due to subsidence of a block, while the blocks adjacent to the subsidence gets uplifted creating ranges.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Normal faults are on both sides the blocks; creating alternating elevated or subsided blocks, otherwise known as horst and graben.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" Basins and ranges can also be formed by blocks that are tilted causing one side to subside while the other side gets uplifted.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" These only have one side with a normal fault, this is known as tilted block faulting.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" Extension causes the plate to stretch, fracture and thin.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":11,"text":" Mountains rise and valleys drop, over a long period of time creating what we see as basin and range topography.","title":"Basin and range topography"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"New Haven-style pizza, locally known as apizza ( , from Neapolitan "’a pizza" (] ) "the pizza"), is a style of Neapolitan pizza common in and around New Haven, Connecticut.","title":"New Haven-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It originated at the Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana and is now served in many other pizza restaurants in the area, most notably Sally's Apizza and Modern Apizza.","title":"New Haven-style pizza"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" This geographically limited pizza style has been favorably referenced by national critics.","title":"New Haven-style pizza"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Yes
